            "type": "output_text",
            "text": "**The latest major release from xAI is Grok 4.6**, which launched on August 12, 2026.[[1]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n\n### Key Details on Grok 4.6\n- It focuses on improvements for **long-running agents**, coding, knowledge work, interactive/visual tasks, and a 500,000-token context window.\n- On the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, it scored approximately **60.92–61**, nearly tying OpenAI's GPT-5.6 Sol Max (one of the top frontier models at the time).[[1]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n- Pricing is listed at **$2 per million input tokens** and **$6 per million output tokens**.\n- It has been rolled out across multiple platforms, including:\n  - GitHub Copilot (August 14, 2026)\n  - Amazon Bedrock\n  - Microsoft Foundry\n  - Google Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform / Vertex AI\n- Additional related releases around the same period include **Grok Bot** (an always-on agent system) and updates to image/video generation (Imagine 2.0 and Video 1.5).[[2]](https://r.jina.ai/https:/x.ai/blog)\n\n### Upcoming: Grok 4.7\nOn September 2, 2026, Elon Musk announced that **Grok 4.7** is expected in about **10 days** (around September 12, 2026). Key highlights include:\n- Scaling up to **2.1 trillion parameters** (from 1.5T in 4.6).\n- Training that incorporates unique **SpaceX data** for superior real-world engineering performance.\n- Musk claims it will **\"exceed all current models\"** while being slightly slower but more token-efficient.[[3]](https://cryptorank.io/news/feed/db1bc-grok-4-7-release-spacex-data)\n\nThis rapid release cadence (4.5 in July, 4.6 in August, 4.7 imminent) reflects xAI's aggressive iteration strategy. For the most up-to-date official information, check [x.ai](https://x.ai) or Elon Musk's/X announcements.",
